What was imported
------------------
CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json, cmake/, src/, include/, ggml/, common/,
tools/, vendor/, gguf-py/, conversion/, grammars/, requirements/, scripts/,
convert_hf_to_gguf.py, LICENSE, licenses/ — verbatim, from
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp at the pinned commit.

NOT vendored: models/ (test-fixture GGUFs), docs/, tests/, benches/,
examples/, pocs/, app/, media/ — this repo's own tests cover the
GreenBoost-side integration instead (same exclusion policy as
synapse_engine/NOTICE). `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS`/`LLAMA_BUILD_EXAMPLES`/
`LLAMA_BUILD_APP` are passed =OFF at configure time by
gb_synapse.build_engine() since these excluded directories are exactly
what those CMake options gate — they default ON in a standalone build
(LLAMA_STANDALONE), so the OFF flags are load-bearing, not cosmetic:
without them cmake fails looking for the missing add_subdirectory() paths.

`scripts/` was NOT in the original prune list and had to be added after a
real `cmake --build` against the pruned tree failed — `tools/ui` (part of
`llama-server`) needs `scripts/ui-assets.cmake` to build its embedded web
UI. Verified 2026-07-24: a full `cmake --build` of all four targets
(llama-server, llama-cli, ggml-rpc-server, llama-quantize) against this
exact pruned tree succeeds and all four binaries run.

